write $-\\frac{2}{3}$ as $-\\frac{4}{6}$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{4}{6}-\\frac{11}{6}=\\frac{-4-11}{6}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $-4-11$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/69/69aec22c2950768abf58a2cae84d3b90a52c79ad44e60d0008605feca272357e.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{-4-11}{6}=\\frac{-15}{6}=-\\frac{15}{6}.\n$$\n\nNow, we simplify:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{15}{6}=-\\frac{15÷3}{6÷3}=-\\frac{5}{2}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{5}{2}=-2\\,\\frac{1}{2}\n$$" 13194139534910 17592186045417 true] [17592186179934 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534910 17592186045417 true] [17592186179934 1071 "Calculate the value of $\\frac{1}{6} - \\frac{3}{8}$." 13194139534910 17592186045417 false] [17592186179934 1071 "Calculate the value of $\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{3}{8}.$" 13194139534910 17592186045417 true] [17592186179934 1074 "We write $\\frac{1}{6}$ as $\\frac{4}{24}$ and $\\frac{3}{8}$ as $\\frac{9}{24},$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{24}-\\frac{9}{24}=\\frac{4-9}{24}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $4-9$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/3f/3f5b60548cfd0332c74508678de51481f9fa149466c7d7880217b905e4d3891a.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{4-9}{24}=\\frac{-5}{24}=-\\frac{5}{24}.\n$$" 13194139534910 17592186045417 true] [17592186180188 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534910 17592186045417 true] [17592186180188 1071 "$1-\\frac{4}{3}=$" 13194139534910 17592186045417 true] [17592186180188 1071 "What is $1 - \\frac{4}{3}$?" 13194139534910 17592186045417 false] [17592186180188 1074 "We write $1$ as $\\frac{3}{3}$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{3}-\\frac{4}{3}=\\frac{3-4}{3}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $3-4$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/42/42e6892273d3fda0560a9b0102077494944812b1e6b66e0bc96af2f0dd2c22c7.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{3-4}{3}=\\frac{-1}{3}=-\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$" 13194139534910 17592186045417 true] [17592186180667 1064 "How can we subtract fractions, like\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2}{4} - \\dfrac{5}{4}\n$$\n\nSince both fractions have the same denominator ($4$), we can combine them into one fraction.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{2}{4} - \\frac{5}{4} &= \\frac{2 - 5}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $2-5$ using our number line:\n\n![](images/c6/c63a3db44b79e751c7cf1a49dcebcbb1d00cea0427da4ef271d07646e4be2748.png)\n\nWe get $2-5=-3$, and therefore\n\n$$\n\\frac{2 - 5}{4} = \\frac{-3}{4} =-\\frac{3}{4}\n$$\n\n**Note:** If two fractions have different denominators, we need to put them over a common denominator *first* and *then* subtract!" 13194139534910 17592186045417 false] [17592186180667 1064 "How can we subtract fractions, like $\\dfrac{2}{4} - \\dfrac{5}{4}?$\n\nSince both fractions have the same denominator ($4$), we can combine them into one fraction.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{4}-\\frac{5}{4} & =\\frac{2-5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $2-5$ using our number line:\n\n![](images/c6/c63a3db44b79e751c7cf1a49dcebcbb1d00cea0427da4ef271d07646e4be2748.png)\n\nWe get $2-5=-3,$ and therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2-5}{4}=\\frac{-3}{4}=-\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** If two fractions have different denominators, we need to put them over a common denominator *first* and *then* subtract!" 13194139534910 17592186045417 true] [17592186443731 1080 "-\\frac{2}{15}" 13194139534910 17592186045417 true] [17592186443731 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534910 17592186045417 true] [17592186443731 1083 #uuid "06826022-9aca-5119-b4b0-e4cd562a853b" 13194139534910 17592186045417 true] [17592186443732 1080 "1" 13194139534910 17592186045417 true] [17592186443732 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534910 17592186045417 true] [17592186443732 1083 #uuid "08e25748-bc23-5fb1-b630-aafea4a149b9" 13194139534910 17592186045417 true] [17592186443733 1080 "1" 13194139534910 17592186045417 true] [17592186443733 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 1